// TestRecsRoundtrip — recommendation-sorting 5.1, the Tier-1 joint: enrich →
// watch → janitor apply → scored serve, every hop a REAL instance (real scan
// through the api route, real serial-scanner + serial-parser + frame-grabber +
// shikimori plugin SUBPROCESSES, the real enrich queue over the real FetchGate,
// the real store ledger/weight txs, the real scored serve handlers over real
// HTTP). shikimori.io stands in NEVER: an httptest stub serves the anime
// payloads and the core-side fetch is pointed at it by rewriting the
// shikimori.io host at the transport — the one injection the black-box joint
// allows (the qa_shikimori_joint posture; the fetch runs in-process, so the
// rewrite reaches it). Coverage referenced, not re-proven: the score model's
// tiers/cap/tiebreak (internal/recs/recs_test.go), the ledger/weight
// primitives (internal/store/recs_test.go), the detector's unit probes
// (cmd/mellifera/recs_probes_test.go), the scored-ordering goldens
// (internal/api/recs_golden_test.go).
//
// What ONLY a joint can prove is asserted here: genres flow through the real
// metadata chain onto the series documents and BOTH consumers resolve them —
// the janitor's enrich resolver (learning write side) and the api namer's own
// projection (serving read side); a ≥90% progress PUT through the real route
// lands the completion ledger row; the wake-poked learning pass raises exactly
// the watched series' genre weights; and the learned weights still land on the
// wire (rec_score), while the served ORDER answers to the watched partition
// (watched-states D4): the completed series sinks below the unweighted
// unwatched one. The watched-states pins ride the same live wire: the
// completed watch withdraws from the default continue rail and
// ?include=watched restores it stamped; the series `watched` flag lands when
// the last episode completes; an explicit `completed: true` intent ledgers
// below the floor; and an unknown `include` value is a 400. The completion
// ledger's idempotency is re-asserted at the joint level: a rewatch crossing
// 90% again inserts nothing, applies nothing, and moves no weight (the second
// pass finds an empty derived queue).
//
// cmd/mellifera is package main and cannot be imported, so its thin-shell
// snippets on this loop are mirrored here in miniature (the harness contract,
// pbSweep precedent): the watch-detect leg of Deps.OnProgress, the recs wake
// channel + janitor select loop, and the recs sweep (queue read → enrich tag
// resolver → ApplyTagWeights tx). Every module boundary those snippets JOIN is
// the production code under test — the mirrors wire only real store, real
// registry, and the real enrich.ResolveGenres/ResolveGates. The thumb re-grab
// leg of the fan-out is out of this joint's scope (its behavior is covered by
// cmd/mellifera's own tests); OnProgress carries the detector leg alone, the
// shape main.go's fanOut composes it into.
